'''truss''' (trus), ''a.'' [< ''truss'', ''n.''] Bunchy; stumpy; stocky; round and thick.
{{smaller block|The tiger-cat is about the bigness of a bull-dog, with short legs, and a ''truss'' body, shaped much like a mastiff.
{{right|''Dampier'', Voyages, an. 1676.}}}}

'''truss-beam''' (trus′bēm), ''n.'' A wooden beam reinforced by a tie-rod, or a compound wooden beam composed of two or more wooden members and reinforced by means of a tie-rod, or a built-up beam of iron arranged in the form of a truss. {{smaller|The most simple form is a single piece of timber having an iron tie-rod on the under side secured at}}

